***************************** T A L Y S **************************4125 1451  144
                                                                  4125 1451  145
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   4125 1451  146
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      4125 1451  147
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    4125 1451  148
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     4125 1451  149
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  4125 1451  150
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        4125 1451  151
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    4125 1451  152
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         4125 1451  153
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      4125 1451  154
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    4125 1451  155
stored in this data file:                                         4125 1451  156
                                                                  4125 1451  157
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   4125 1451  158
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     4125 1451  159
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 4125 1451  160
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   4125 1451  161
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                4125 1451  162
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   4125 1451  163
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    4125 1451  164
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        4125 1451  165
- Recoil data                                                     4125 1451  166
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           4125 1451  167
- Total particle energy spectra                                   4125 1451  168
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      4125 1451  169
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        4125 1451  170
- Residual production cross sections                              4125 1451  171
                                                                  4125 1451  172
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            4125 1451  173
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        4125 1451  174
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   4125 1451  175
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                4125 1451  176
                                                                  4125 1451  177
