##### MF1: GENERAL INFORMATION                                    4125 1451  180
                                                                  4125 1451  181
- MT451    : Descriptive data and directory                       4125 1451  182
                                                                  4125 1451  183
This text and the full directory of used MF/MT sections.          4125 1451  184
                                                                  4125 1451  185
##### MF2: RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                   4125 1451  186
                                                                  4125 1451  187
- MT151    : Resonance parameters                                 4125 1451  188
                                                                  4125 1451  189
Details about the origin of the resonance parameters for this     4125 1451  190
nuclide are given above in this description. In general, both a   4125 1451  191
Resolved and an Unresolved Resonance Range are given.             4125 1451  192
                                                                  4125 1451  193
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                4125 1451  194
                                                                  4125 1451  195
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       4125 1451  196
calculated with TALYS, possibly normalized to experimental data.  4125 1451  197
If the maximal cross section in an excitation function over the   4125 1451  198
whole energy range does not exceed 1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not  4125 1451  199
included. Cross sections lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have  4125 1451  200
no physical meaning and are set to zero. All MT numbers extend up 4125 1451  201
to the highest incident energy.                                   4125 1451  202
The following reaction channels/MT numbers are generally included:4125 1451  203
                                                                  4125 1451  204
- MT1      : Total cross section                                  4125 1451  205
                                                                  4125 1451  206
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range,    4125 1451  207
or partly reproduced using experimental data.                     4125 1451  208
                                                                  4125 1451  209
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section                     4125 1451  210
                                                                  4125 1451  211
Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section from the    4125 1451  212
total cross section.                                              4125 1451  213
                                                                  4125 1451  214
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            4125 1451  215
                                                                  4125 1451  216
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    4125 1451  217
                                                                  4125 1451  218
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        4125 1451  219
                                                                  4125 1451  220
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  4125 1451  221
                                                                  4125 1451  222
- MT5      : (n,anything) cross section                           4125 1451  223
                                                                  4125 1451  224
MT5 contains the reactions which can not be stored in any other   4125 1451  225
MT-number. The information of MF3/MT5 can be combined with        4125 1451  226
MF6/MT5 to obtain residual production cross sections particle     4125 1451  227
production cross sections and (double-)differential cross         4125 1451  228
sections.                                                         4125 1451  229
                                                                  4125 1451  230
- MT16     : (n,2n) cross section                                 4125 1451  231
- MT17     : (n,3n) cross section                                 4125 1451  232
- MT22     : (n,na) cross section                                 4125 1451  233
- MT28     : (n,np) cross section                                 4125 1451  234
- MT51-90  : (n,n') cross section for 1st-40th excited state      4125 1451  235
- MT91     : (n,n') continuum cross section                       4125 1451  236
- MT102    : (n,gamma) cross section                              4125 1451  237
- MT103    : (n,p) cross section                                  4125 1451  238
- MT104    : (n,d) cross section                                  4125 1451  239
- MT105    : (n,t) cross section                                  4125 1451  240
- MT106    : (n,h) cross section                                  4125 1451  241
- MT107    : (n,a) cross section                                  4125 1451  242
- MT600-610: (n,p) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       4125 1451  243
- MT649    : (n,p) continuum cross section                        4125 1451  244
- MT650-655: (n,d) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        4125 1451  245
- MT699    : (n,d) continuum cross section                        4125 1451  246
- MT700-705: (n,t) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        4125 1451  247
- MT749    : (n,t) continuum cross section                        4125 1451  248
- MT750-755: (n,h) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        4125 1451  249
- MT799    : (n,h) continuum cross section                        4125 1451  250
- MT800-810: (n,a) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       4125 1451  251
- MT849    : (n,a) continuum cross section                        4125 1451  252
                                                                  4125 1451  253
##### MF4: ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY PARTICLES           4125 1451  254
                                                                  4125 1451  255
We use MF4 for the neutron scattering angular distribution for    4125 1451  256
discrete levels.                                                  4125 1451  257
                                                                  4125 1451  258
- MT2      : Elastic angular distribution                         4125 1451  259
                                                                  4125 1451  260
The flag LTT=3 is used to indicate a switch at some high energy,  4125 1451  261
generally 50 MeV, from a Legendre representation to a tabulated   4125 1451  262
representation. For incident energies below this energy, the      4125 1451  263
Legendre coefficients are given on a sufficiently precise energy  4125 1451  264
grid. They are a sum of calculated Legendre coefficients for      4125 1451  265
compound nucleus and shape-elastic scattering. For higher         4125 1451  266
incident energies, relative angular distributions are tabulated   4125 1451  267
on an angular grid.                                               4125 1451  268
                                                                  4125 1451  269
- MT51-70  : (n,n') angular distribution for 1st-20th state       4125 1451  270
- MT600-610: (n,p) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        4125 1451  271
- MT650-655: (n,d) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         4125 1451  272
- MT700-705: (n,t) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         4125 1451  273
- MT750-755: (n,h) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         4125 1451  274
- MT800-810: (n,a) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        4125 1451  275
                                                                  4125 1451  276
##### MF6: PRODUCT ENERGY-ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS                     4125 1451  277
                                                                  4125 1451  278
In MF6 we store all secondary energy, angle, and energy-angle     4125 1451  279
distributions, as well as all residual and discrete + continuum   4125 1451  280
photon production cross sections for channels other than capture  4125 1451  281
(MT102) and reactions to discrete levels (MT51,etc.).             4125 1451  282
All data are generated with TALYS.                                4125 1451  283
                                                                  4125 1451  284
- MT5      : (n,anything) yields and energy-angle distributions   4125 1451  285
                                                                  4125 1451  286
MT5 contains, in this order,                                      4125 1451  287
For neutrons up to alpha particles and photons:                   4125 1451  288
- the production yields per particle for the whole energy range   4125 1451  289
- the secondary energy-angle distributions per particles which are4125 1451  290
  not represented by explicit MT numbers. On a secondary energy   4125 1451  291
  grid the relative emission spectra are given together with the  4125 1451  292
  parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular              4125 1451  293
  distributions. Inelastic scattering cross sections for discrete 4125 1451  294
  states have been broadened and added to the continuum spectra.  4125 1451  295
For each residual product:                                        4125 1451  296
- the production yields for the whole energy range.               4125 1451  297
- the recoil                                                      4125 1451  298
These distributions can be multiplied with MF3/MT5 to get         4125 1451  299
the production cross sections and (double-)differential cross     4125 1451  300
sections.                                                         4125 1451  301
                                                                  4125 1451  302
- MT16     : (n,2n) energy-angle distr. and photon production     4125 1451  303
                                                                  4125 1451  304
First, for each type of outgoing particle, the (trivial) integer  4125 1451  305
particle yields are given. Next, on a sufficiently dense incident 4125 1451  306
energy grid the secondary energy-angle distributions are          4125 1451  307
specified by means of the relative emission spectra and the       4125 1451  308
parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular distributions. 4125 1451  309
Next, the photon yield is tabulated as a function of incident     4125 1451  310
energy. For each incident energy, the photon production is given  4125 1451  311
for all discrete gamma lines present in the final nucleus. A      4125 1451  312
continuum photon distribution is added to this. We assume         4125 1451  313
isotropy for all produced gamma rays.                             4125 1451  314
                                                                  4125 1451  315
For the following MT-numbers, the same procedure as for MT16 is   4125 1451  316
followed:                                                         4125 1451  317
                                                                  4125 1451  318
- MT17 : (n,3n) energy-angle distr. and photon production         4125 1451  319
- MT22 : (n,na) energy-angle distr. and photon production         4125 1451  320
- MT28 : (n,np) energy-angle distr. and photon production         4125 1451  321
- MT91 : (n,n') continuum energy-angle distr. and phot. prod.     4125 1451  322
- MT649: (n,p) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     4125 1451  323
- MT699: (n,d) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     4125 1451  324
- MT749: (n,t) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     4125 1451  325
- MT809: (n,h) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     4125 1451  326
- MT849: (n,a) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     4125 1451  327
                                                                  4125 1451  328
##### MF8: RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                 4125 1451  329
                                                                  4125 1451  330
For reactions to isomers, MF8 designates where the information    4125 1451  331
for isomeric versus ground state production, or residual          4125 1451  332
production can be found, i.e. for each MT number it points to     4125 1451  333
either MF6, MF9 or MF10.                                          4125 1451  334
                                                                  4125 1451  335
##### MF9: MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES  4125 1451  336
                                                                  4125 1451  337
MF9 is used for isomer production by non-threshold reactions.     4125 1451  338
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    4125 1451  339
as isomer.                                                        4125 1451  340
                                                                  4125 1451  341
##### MF10: CROSS SECTIONS FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES 4125 1451  342
                                                                  4125 1451  343
MF10 is used for isomer production by threshold reactions.        4125 1451  344
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    4125 1451  345
as isomer.                                                        4125 1451  346
                                                                  4125 1451  347
##### MF12: PHOTON PRODUCTION YIELD DATA                          4125 1451  348
                                                                  4125 1451  349
MF12 is used for the photon production for two types of reactions:4125 1451  350
- Reactions to discrete levels (MT51, etc.) For this transition   4125 1451  351
  probabilities are used (LO=2)                                   4125 1451  352
- Photons from neutron capture (MT102). Here multiplicities are   4125 1451  353
  given                                                           4125 1451  354
                                                                  4125 1451  355
##### MF14: PHOTON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                          4125 1451  356
                                                                  4125 1451  357
All photon production is considered as isotropic                  4125 1451  358
                                                                  4125 1451  359
##### MF15: PHOTON ENERGY SPECTRA                                 4125 1451  360
                                                                  4125 1451  361
For capture (MT102), the photon energy spectrum is given.         4125 1451  362
                                                                  4125 1451  363
##### MF32: COVARIANCES OF RESONANCE PARAMETERS                   4125 1451  364
                                                                  4125 1451  365
In MF32, we store the covariances of resonance parameters,        4125 1451  366
and more details are given above in this description. In most     4125 1451  367
versions of TENDL, this information is now stored in MF33.        4125 1451  368
                                                                  4125 1451  369
##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 4125 1451  370
                                                                  4125 1451  371
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  4125 1451  372
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     4125 1451  373
with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates TALYS runs using    4125 1451  374
a Monte Carlo parameter method.                                   4125 1451  375
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  4125 1451  376
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                4125 1451  377
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      4125 1451  378
   same reaction channel between different energies)              4125 1451  379
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      4125 1451  380
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               4125 1451  381
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      4125 1451  382
   different reaction channels for different energies)            4125 1451  383
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        4125 1451  384
flag LB=5, followed by a LB=8 section which contains              4125 1451  385
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3. Next, classes 3  4125 1451  386
and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to account for the different       4125 1451  387
energy grids that two correlating MT-sections may have. Since     4125 1451  388
the total correlation matrix is fully symmetric, we only need to  4125 1451  389
include the correlation elements between different MT-numbers     4125 1451  390
once, and we do that in the subsection with the lowest of the     4125 1451  391
two MT-numbers. We include covariance information for all the     4125 1451  392
total cross sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the   4125 1451  393
individual inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do   4125 1451  394
not include covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers. For the  4125 1451  395
most important channels, we include cross-channel correlations.   4125 1451  396
                                                                  4125 1451  397
##### MF34: COVARIANCES OF ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                  4125 1451  398
                                                                  4125 1451  399
In MF34, we store the covariances of the elastic scattering       4125 1451  400
angular distributions that are given in MF4/MT2. All covariances  4125 1451  401
are generated with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates       4125 1451  402
TALYS runs using a Monte Carlo parameter method. The tables are   4125 1451  403
restricted to MT2 and contain covariances for the first 6         4125 1451  404
Legendre coefficients. Both intra- and inter-correlations of the  4125 1451  405
various Legendre coefficients are given. As in MF33, the LB5      4125 1451  406
representation is used.                                           4125 1451  407
                                                                  4125 1451  408
##### MF40: COVARIANCES OF ISOMER PRODUCTION                      4125 1451  409
                                                                  4125 1451  410
For covariances of ground state and isomeric cross sections, the  4125 1451  411
